Error [E2307]: `text` cannot be stored in a struct field without an owning copy
  --> zero_copy_parser_rejects_locally_owned_source.jet:11:25
    |
 11 |     return Token{ text: text, rest: rest }
    |                         ^^^^
 Why: `text` is a zero-copy view into `source` (`.trim()`/`.after()`/`.before()`); this destination needs an owned `String`, and `copies: .Explicit` keeps the implicit materialization disabled
 Fix: Write `~text` first, or remove `copies: .Explicit` to use the default owning copy
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2307

Error [E2307]: `rest` cannot be stored in a struct field without an owning copy
  --> zero_copy_parser_rejects_locally_owned_source.jet:11:37
    |
 11 |     return Token{ text: text, rest: rest }
    |                                     ^^^^
 Why: `rest` is a zero-copy view into `source` (`.trim()`/`.after()`/`.before()`); this destination needs an owned `String`, and `copies: .Explicit` keeps the implicit materialization disabled
 Fix: Write `~rest` first, or remove `copies: .Explicit` to use the default owning copy
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2307

Error [E2305]: This view points into `source`, which this function owns
  --> zero_copy_parser_rejects_locally_owned_source.jet:11:25
    |
 11 |     return Token{ text: text, rest: rest }
    |                         ^^^^
 Why: `source` is made here and freed when the function returns, so a read window into it would outlive what owns it — there'd be nothing left to look at
 Fix: Return an owned copy with `place.copy()` (for example `value[a..b].copy()`), or accept the source as a parameter so the caller keeps owning it
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2305

